  <entry>
    <id>tag:github.com,2008:Grit::Commit/876a61ddd5782a45e55374148341086678ce91d4</id>
    <link type="text/html" rel="alternate" href="https://github.com/caocaochan/hydcd-yomitan/commit/876a61ddd5782a45e55374148341086678ce91d4"/>
    <title>
        Strip literal corner brackets from fw-edition quotes
    </title>
    <updated>2026-09-11T21:49:25Z</updated>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6279168?s=30&amp;v=4"/>
    <author>
      <name>Fighter1</name>
      <uri>https://github.com/Fighter1</uri>
    </author>
    <content type="html">
      &lt;pre style=&#39;white-space:pre-wrap;width:81ex&#39;&gt;Strip literal corner brackets from fw-edition quotes

The 光盘2.0 edition records (&amp;lt;hdcs class=&amp;quot;fw&amp;quot;&amp;gt;) write 「」 as literal text
inside &amp;lt;quote&amp;gt; elements, and the source stylesheet suppresses its own
pseudo-element brackets for that class. The converter drops the root
class during sanitization and the packaged CSS brackets every quote, so
those entries rendered doubled brackets such as 「「修」」 for 俢.

Remove a wrapping 「…」 pair from quote content at conversion time and
report the count as quote_literal_brackets_stripped. This affects 107
quotes across 64 headwords in the pinned 2025.12.13 source. Quotes that
carry curly “” quotes are left untouched, since that is source
punctuation rather than a duplicate.&lt;/pre&gt;
    </content>
  </entry>
